// Title: Disable Privacy Settings Experience in Registry
// Sigma ID: 0372e1f9-0fd2-40f7-be1b-a7b2b848fa7b
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-10-02 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects registry modifications that disable Privacy Settings Experience
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate admin script
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/9e5b12c4912c07562aec7500447b11fa3e17e254/atomics/T1562.001/T1562.001.md
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_disable_privacy_settings_experience.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\OOBE\\DisablePrivacyExperience" and RegistryValueData =~ "DWORD (0x00000000)"
